      "text": "Since $\\sin E = 1$, we have $E = 90^{\\circ}$.  Thus, $F = 90^{\\circ} - D$.  Therefore, $\\sin F = \\sin (90^{\\circ} - D)$.  Since $\\sin (90^{\\circ} - \\theta) = \\cos \\theta$, this implies that $\\sin F = \\cos D$.  Therefore, $\\sin F = \\boxed{\\frac{12}{13}}$. The answer is \\frac{12}{13}",
